      "writtenOn": "2024-01-05T21:37:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The sensor is actually binding to S3 rails on Corsola. However, the rail is from AP PMIC. When AP issues a shutdown command, the PMIC would turn it off immediately in S0, and then EC is aware of the S0-\u003eS3 transition later. This would cause the i2c communication to fail while setting the data rate to 0 in S0-\u003eS3 transition. \n\nDo you have any other suggestion for this one?",
      "parentUuid": "dc942192_b76926a2",
      "revId": "d078f6cd5331047d81d3b5fd93822d476fc26561",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
